.TH MEMFLUSH 1 "November 2026" "memflush 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memflush \- Advanced Linux memory compaction and cache flush utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memflush
[\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-no\-notify\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-silent\fR|\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmemflush\fR proactively defragments memory zones, compresses dormant cold process pages into \fBZRAM\fR swap, and safely flushes unused file page caches, directory entries (dentries), and inodes.
.PP
Unlike traditional cache-dropping scripts that only flush page caches, \fBmemflush\fR interacts directly with modern Linux kernel cgroup v2 interfaces (\fI/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.reclaim\fR) and kernel memory compaction (\fI/proc/sys/vm/compact_memory\fR).
.PP
\fBmemflush\fR requires elevated privileges to perform memory reclaim. It integrates seamlessly with \fBsystemd\fR, Polkit, and sudoers rules to allow passwordless execution from user sessions and desktop keybindings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-no\-notify\fR
Run in terminal output mode only. Skips desktop notifications via \fBnotify\-send\fR. Useful for SSH sessions, scripts, and headless servers.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-silent\fR
Run completely silent. Suppresses all terminal text and desktop notifications. Ideal for desktop keyboard shortcuts and window manager autostart hooks.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Alias for \fB\-\-silent\fR.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display usage information and exit.
.SH EXECUTION LIFECYCLE
When invoked, \fBmemflush\fR executes in three stages:
.IP 1. 3
\fBProactive CGroup Reclaim:\fR Writes to \fI/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.reclaim\fR to push inactive, cold anonymous pages into ZRAM swap.
.IP 2. 3
\fBZone Compaction:\fR Triggers proactive memory zone defragmentation via \fI/proc/sys/vm/compact_memory\fR to satisfy high-order kernel allocations.
.IP 3. 3
\fBCache Flushing:\fR Syncs dirty pages to disk and clears page caches, dentries, and inodes via \fI/proc/sys/vm/drop_caches\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/usr/local/bin/memflush\fR (or \fI/usr/bin/memflush\fR)
The primary executable binary.
.TP
\fI/etc/systemd/system/memflush.service\fR
Hardened systemd unit file providing elevated execution without interactive authentication.
.TP
\fI/etc/polkit\-1/rules.d/99\-memflush.rules\fR
Polkit authorization rule allowing members of the \fBwheel\fR and \fBsudo\fR groups to start \fBmemflush.service\fR without password prompts.
.TP
\fI/etc/sudoers.d/memflush\fR
Fallback sudoers configuration for passwordless service execution.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Standard interactive execution with terminal statistics and desktop notification:
.RS
.B memflush
.RE
.PP
Run in terminal without sending a desktop notification:
.RS
.B memflush \-\-no\-notify
.RE
.PP
Silent execution from a desktop keybinding (e.g. Hyprland, Sway, KDE):
.RS
.B memflush \-\-silent
.RE
.PP
Automatic boot cleanup (execute 8 seconds after login in autostart):
.RS
.B sh \-c 'sleep 8 && memflush \-\-silent'
.RE
